## Constraints

<The rules Claude would otherwise break. Each one states what is forbidden and why, in one
or two lines. Delete the ones that do not apply to this project.>

**Git.** Do not run `git commit`, `git push`, `git rebase`, `git merge` or `git reset`
without explicit approval in the conversation. Ask first, every time.

**Python environment.** All Python runs through the project virtual environment
(`.venv`), never the system interpreter. Installing a dependency needs approval first.

**Migrations.** Create them only with `alembic revision --autogenerate -m "..."`. Never
hand-write one; a hand-edited migration desyncs the chain and breaks upgrades in production.

**Hardware pins.** Before touching GPIO or wiring, read `<path to the pin map>`. It is the
source of truth. Do not guess pin numbers; update that document in the same task when a pin
changes.

